{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Presenting the Product", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Meeting Etiquette", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 1, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 14, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Explain customs and appropriate behaviour at work and in different countries, using a wider range of expressions and formulas. ", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Expressing Advice", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " There are many different ways to make recommendations and express advice. The modal verbs \"had better\", \"ought to\" and \"might\" are often used to make recommendations. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Had better</span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "a. Form: subject + had better + bare infinitive (verb without \u2018to')", "type": "text"}, {"content": "b. Meaning: \u201chad better\u201d is very similar in meaning to should but it is stronger because it implies a negative consequence if the advice is not followed. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Ought to</span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "a. Form: subject + ought to + bare infinitive (verb without \u2018to')", "type": "text"}, {"content": "b. Meaning: \u201cought to\u201d is used for saying what you think is the right thing to do. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Might </span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "a. Form: subject + might + bare infinitive (verb without \u2018to')", "type": "text"}, {"content": "b. Meaning: \u201cmight\u201d is used for making a suggestion or recommendation. It's not as strong as \u201chad better\u201d. We commonly use the verb \u201chave\u201d with \u201cmight\u201d. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You <span class=\"underline\">might want</span>  to take a seat and listen to what I have to say. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I thought you <span class=\"underline\">might want</span>  to see what I have done.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I have a meeting so we <span class=\"underline\">ought to</span>  keep this chat short. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You<span class=\"underline\">'d better</span>  get your act together now. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We <span class=\"underline\">ought to do</span>  something about this. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "This problem <span class=\"underline\">had better</span>  be addressed before we lose everything. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We <span class=\"underline\">ought to</span> come up with a swift response. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Dealing With a Difficult Customer", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " Dealing with difficult customers is requires a skillful use of language. Here are some expressions you can use to defuse a situation when dealing with angry customers. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Customer </span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Making the complaint</span> <ul><li>I'm sorry, but I'm not satisfied with ...</li> <li>I've been ... </li> <li>I am very dissatisfied with the service I received. </li></ul> <span class=\"strong\">Insisting</span> <ul><li>It really isn't good enough / It's not enough. </li><li>I'd like to know why ...</li></ul> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Dealing with Complaints </span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Showing understanding</span> <ul><li>I truly understand your concerns. </li><li>I completely understand ...</li> <li>I apologise for ...</li> <li>I understand you're upset about ... </li> <li>We appreciated the feedback. </li> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Understanding the situation</span><ul> <li>Could you give me some details, please?</li> </ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Promising action</span><ul><li>We ought to come up with a plan. </li> <li>We might want to approach this differently. </li> </ul>", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "stand-up meeting", "type": "name"}, {"content": " meeting in which participants stand in order to keep it short", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I have a stand-up meeting with my team shortly.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le14ob01aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about a meeting.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "keep it brief", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be concise; to avoid talking a long time", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We ought to keep it brief. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le14ob01aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "get your act together", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to organize yourself in order to be more effective", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They had better get their act together and do something about this. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le14ob01aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "dissatisfied (with)", "type": "name"}, {"content": "not pleased with something or someone", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm very dissatisfied with the service I received.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le14ob01aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to alleviate", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to make a problem or injury less severe", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The press release was supposed to alleviate the crisis.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le14ob01aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to get bombarded", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to be attacked repeatedly", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm getting bombarded by the press. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le14ob01aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "swift response ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a quick reply", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We ought to come up with a swift and appropriate crisis communication response.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le14ob01aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Think of a situation in which you would need to call customer service (e.g. overcharged on your credit card).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Create an imaginary dialogue between a customer and a customer service agent.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use the examples for \u201cmaking a complaint\u201d and \u201cshowing understanding\u201d to begin your sentences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Act out your dialogue with a partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I create a dialogue.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use appropriate language for making a complaint.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use appropriate language for showing understanding.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I practice the dialogue with a partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le14ob01re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}], "labs": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"id": 0, "stimuli_ids": [0], "questions": [], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"cont